1. Executive Summary & Business Value

In regulated banking environments, developer velocity frequently slows down during manual InfoSec, PCI-DSS, and SOX compliance reviews. Catching issues like unmasked PII in logs or missing ledger audit events late in CI/CD creates expensive rework.
Our Solution: A shift-left Pre-Merge PR Gatekeeper powered by Claude Code. Before a developer opens a PR, they run /review-pr. An orchestrator command delegates parallel compliance checks to isolated subagents equipped with internal banking skills, generates a pass/fail compliance report, and safely auto-remediates blockers with test verification hooks.

Key Claude Code Concepts Demonstrated

1. Custom Slash Command (/review-pr): Deterministic main workflow orchestrator.
2. Isolated Subagents (.claude/agents/): Parallel, read-only auditors (pci-pii-auditor, sox-audit-checker, sec-config-auditor) that keep the main context window clean.
3. Domain Skills (.claude/skills/): Reusable banking compliance standards (SKILL.md) automatically applied during audits and fixes.
4. Lifecycle Hooks (.claude/settings.json): Automated test/lint guardrails that run after any code modification to ensure self-healing fixes don't break builds.

