# Banking Engineering Compliance Standards

## 1. PCI-DSS & PII Data Protection (CRITICAL)
- **Never** log raw Primary Account Numbers (PAN), SSNs, routing numbers, or customer full names.
- All account/card numbers in logs must use `MaskingUtil.maskAccount(value)` showing only the last 4 digits (`****1234`).
- Exception stack traces must not expose raw request payloads containing customer DTOs.

## 2. SOX Financial Integrity & Auditability (CRITICAL)
- Every state-changing financial endpoint (`POST /transfer`, `POST /debit`, `POST /credit`) **must**:
  1. Require and validate an `X-Idempotency-Key` header.
  2. Emit an immutable structured event via `AuditEventPublisher.publish(...)` containing `transactionId`, `actorId`, `timestamp`, and `amount`.

## 3. Application Security & Cryptography (HIGH)
- Hardcoded API keys, tokens, or credentials are strictly prohibited.
- Deprecated cryptographic algorithms (`MD5`, `SHA-1`, `DES`, `ECB` mode) are banned; use `SHA-256` or `AES-GCM`.
- Outbound HTTP clients must enforce TLS 1.2+.
